+
+## Evaluation of the planner's actual forecast
+
+The headline forecast table above describes the saved **rank ensemble** from the earlier run. The funding planner exports a different calculation: an average of model probabilities, each rescaled to the training onset rate. These are now evaluated separately using one shared forecast function.
+
+Run `python pipeline/evaluate_planner.py --bootstrap 1000` after downloading the risk workbooks and extra datasets. It evaluates the full model within baseline At-Risk systems as well as all non-Failing systems, compares against the SAFER risk score and a training-only status-rate baseline, and checks annual probability calibration. It performs no test-year model selection or recalibration.
+
+See [PLANNER_EVALUATION.md](PLANNER_EVALUATION.md) for the results and qualifications. Exact inputs, hashes, settings and versions are in `data/planner_evaluation.json`; held-out predictions are in `data/planner_test_predictions.csv`. The command does not regenerate the app's saved forecasts or funding plans. The separate historical-input audit remains necessary before describing these results as prospective, leakage-free performance.
